  "slug": "daring-club-motema-pembe",
  "summary": "DCMP is a Kinshasa football club founded in 1936 by missionary Father Raphaël de la Kethulle, initially as Daring. It became CS Imana in 1949 and adopted the name Daring Club Motéma Pembe in 1985. Developed from teams at Sainte-Anne school, it became the DRC’s most successful club by national titles, with 27 since 1963, including 12 Linafoot championships and a record 14 Congo Cups.\n\nThe club first competed in continental football in 1964 and won the African Cup Winners’ Cup in 1994, defeating Kenya Breweries; it later lost the CAF Super Cup to Espérance de Tunis. Domestic titles followed across several decades, including Linafoot championships in 2004, 2005 and 2008.\n\nIn the 2010s, organizational instability and internal disputes weakened the club. A split in 2014 led to the formation of CS Imana. The club adopted the name Daring Club Motéma Pembe Imana in 2015, and leadership changes in 2016 aimed to restore its competitiveness.",
